* dlnn_board_parts.lib -- part models for the C tier in board mode (dlnn/tiers/circuit_board.py).  M2a.
* Replaces hw/board/lib/dlnn_sim.lib (idealised stand-ins) in the KiCad-exported TILE-8 netlist; subckt names and pin
* orders are those of the exported netlist.  EVERYTHING HERE IS SIMULATION MODEL, NOTHING MEASURED.
*
* Provenance (labels used in the docs/JSON):
*   IND_FH1812   DATASHEET-DERIVED lumped model of FH FHW1812IF121JST (JLC C394134): L 120 uH +-5 %, DCR 3.3 ohm (listing, treated as
*                max), SRF 3.3 MHz -> C_p = 1/((2 pi SRF)^2 L) = 19.38 pF, Q >= 10 @ 796 kHz (listing: MINIMUM) -> R_p such that
*                1/Q = DCR/(wL) + wL/R_p at 796 kHz: 6.351 kohm (Q=10 corner) / 21.56 kohm (Q=30 corner, Q_typ is ASSUMED = 3 x min,
*                not a datasheet value).  Series L + DCR, parallel C_p || R_p across the whole inductor.  Not a vendor model.
*   OPA_QUAD     (opa_quad_ti.lib / opa_quad_fit.lib, one of the two is included) TI's own PSpice macro TLV9062 (SBOMAG1E, Rev D, downloaded at run time from ti.com, not committed), 4 instances per
*                package; TLV9064 is stated to be the same die as TLV9062 (TI e2e); +2 pF input pad on every non-inverting input
*                (design assumption of M1a: c_tap 6 pF = Cic 4 pF + 2 pF).  The macro is a PSpice-dialect model: run with
*                'set ngbehavior=psa'.  The browser export uses a single-pole op-amp instead (docs/artifacts/data/spice).
*   DUAL_NPN     GENERIC NPN fitted to BC847BS datasheet TABLE points (VBE(on) 665 mV @ 2 mA, hFE ~300, CCBO 2 pF, CEBO 11 pF, fT >= 100 MHz);
*                curves not digitised; VAF=100 V, RB=10 ohm, MJ=0.33, VJ=0.75, TF=0.6 ns are ASSUMED.  Same model as hw/board/spice/run_checks.py.
*   SW4066_QUAD  74HCT4066: R_on + C_off.  R_on(T) = 95 ohm + 0.383 ohm/K (T-25 C) (TI CD74HC4066: 95 ohm max @ 25 C, 118 ohm @ 85 C,
*                Vcc 4.5 V; HCT assumed equal), C_off = 5 pF per terminal (ASSUMED, datasheet gives only a 10 pF max input
*                capacitance), no charge injection modelled (the board_design.md 2 pC is an assumption and is not in SPICE).
*   DAC4_IDEAL   MCP4728 output stage as four ideal voltage sources (levels set per run from the model bias, 12-bit quantised).
*   LM4040_25    2.5 V shunt reference as an ideal source (as in the baseline lib).
.param TEMPC=25
.model QNPN_G npn (IS=1.3520e-14 BF=300 VAF=100 RB=10 TF=0.6n CJE=13p CJC=4.8p MJE=0.33 MJC=0.33 VJE=0.75 VJC=0.75)
.subckt IND_FH1812 a b L=120u R=3.3 Cp=19.383p Rp=6350.9
L1 a m {L}
R1 m b {R}
Cp1 a b {Cp}
Rp1 a b {Rp}
.ends IND_FH1812
.subckt DUAL_NPN e1 b1 c2 e2 b2 c1
Q1 c1 b1 e1 QNPN_G
Q2 c2 b2 e2 QNPN_G
.ends DUAL_NPN
.model SW4066 SW (Ron=95 Roff=1e9 Vt=2.5 Vh=0.2)
.subckt SW4066_QUAD a1 b1 e1 a2 b2 e2 a3 b3 e3 a4 b4 e4 vdd vss PARAMS: ron=95
S1 a1 b1 e1 vss SW4066
S2 a2 b2 e2 vss SW4066
S3 a3 b3 e3 vss SW4066
S4 a4 b4 e4 vss SW4066
Ca1 a1 vss 5p
Cb1 b1 vss 5p
Ca2 a2 vss 5p
Cb2 b2 vss 5p
Ca3 a3 vss 5p
Cb3 b3 vss 5p
Ca4 a4 vss 5p
Cb4 b4 vss 5p
Rvdd vdd 0 1e9
.ends SW4066_QUAD
.subckt DAC4_IDEAL vdd scl sda ldac rdy oa ob oc od vss VA=2.5 VB=2.5 VC=2.5 VD=2.5
Va oa vss {VA}
Vb ob vss {VB}
Vc oc vss {VC}
Vd od vss {VD}
Rvdd vdd 0 1e9
Rscl scl 0 1e9
Rsda sda 0 1e9
Rldac ldac 0 1e9
Rrdy rdy 0 1e9
.ends DAC4_IDEAL
.subckt LM4040_25 k a
V1 k a DC 2.5
.ends LM4040_25
